### Test Extended Auth Endpoints

### 1. Register a new user first
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123",
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "User",
  "phoneNumber": "+1234567890"
}

### 2. Login to get token
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "password123"
}

### 3. Get current user info (replace YOUR_TOKEN with actual token from login)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN

### 4. Update password
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "current_password": "password123",
  "new_password": "newpassword456"
}

### 5. Send password reset email
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/forgot-password
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com"
}

### 6. Logout (replace YOUR_TOKEN with actual token)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN

### 7. Delete account (replace YOUR_TOKEN with actual token)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/v1/auth/account
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "token": "YOUR_TOKEN"
}